    "q-293702": {
      "dom_id": "step-q293702",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{3}-2.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{3}-2,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+2} & = \\\\ \\frac{5-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2}{\\sqrt{3}-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(5-\\sqrt{3})(\\sqrt{3}-2)}{(\\sqrt{3}+2)(\\sqrt{3}-2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{3}-10-(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+2\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}-(2)^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{3}-10-3}{3-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{3}-13}{-1} & = \\\\ 13-7\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-293702-a",
